%S A399932 1,1,1,1,1,1,6,5,5,20,16,51,66,124,145,311,364
%N A399932 Maximum number of Hamiltonian cycles in a polyhex with 2*n cells.
%C A399932 The cycles pass from a cell to a neighboring cell, visiting each cell exactly once.
%C A399932 We follow the convention that K_1 and K_2 have 1 Hamiltonian cycle each, so a(1) = a(2) = 1.
%C A399932 For all n <= 17 except for n = 6, there is a unique polyhex (up to rotations and reflections) that admits a(n) Hamiltonian cycles. See linked illustration.
%H A399932 Pontus von Brömssen, <a href="/A399932/a399932.svg">Illustration of all (free) polyhexes with up to 17 cells and the maximum number of Hamiltonian cycles</a>.
%H A399932 <a href="/index/Pol#polyominoes">Index entries for sequences related to polyominoes</a>.
%Y A399932 Cf. A000228, A036418, A399931, A399933.
%K A399932 nonn,more,new
